            "text": "{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The conversation history before this point was compacted into the following summary:\\n\\n<summary>\\n## Goal\\n- Get the current weather in Tokyo using get_weather and answer in one short sentence.\\n\\n## Constraints & Preferences\\n- Use the get_weather tool to retrieve the data.\\n- Answer in one short sentence.\\n\\n## Progress\\n### Done\\n- [x] Called get_weather(city=\\\"Tokyo\\\") and received the result.\\n- [x] Delivered the answer: \\\"Tokyo is clear and 25°C with winds at 10 km/h.\\\"\\n\\n### In Progress\\n- [ ] (none)\\n\\n### Blocked\\n- (none)\\n\\n## Key Decisions\\n- **Used get_weather tool**: The user explicitly requested it as the data source for the weather report.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n1. No further action required unless the user asks for additional weather information or another city.\\n\\n## Critical Context\\n- Tool result: \\\"Tokyo: clear25°C, wind 10 km/h\\\"\\n- Final answer given: \\\"Tokyo is clear and 25°C with winds at 10 km/h.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\\n\\n## Original Request\\nThe user asked: \\\"Is that warm? One word.\\\" They want a one-word answer about whether something is warm. The referent of \\\"that\\\" is not specified in the conversation shown.\\n\\n## Progress So Far\\n- The user posed a single question requesting a one-word reply.\\n- No assistant response appears in the provided messages.\\n- No work or decisions have been made yet.\\n\\n## Context Needed to Continue\\n- The object or thing \\\"that\\\" refers to is not identified in the visible messages, so the temperature question lacks explicit context.\\n- The user expects a one-word answer format.\\n</summary>\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"low\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Yes.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Should I bring an umbrella? One word.\",\"cache_control\":{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"low\"}}],\"max_tokens\":128000,\"stream\":true,\"system\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"You are a weather assistant. Answer briefly.\\n\\n<addendum>\\nReference for pi-restore-anthropic-haiku-5-5-compaction: the weather desk's station catalog. Use it only when asked.\\n- Station 1: code WX001, elevation 0 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 2: code WX002, elevation 37 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 3: code WX003, elevation 74 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 4: code WX004, elevation 111 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 5: code WX005, elevation 148 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 6: code WX006, elevation 185 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 7: code WX007, elevation 222 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 8: code WX008, elevation 259 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 9: code WX009, elevation 296 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 10: code WX010, elevation 333 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 11: code WX011, elevation 370 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 12: code WX012, elevation 407 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 13: code WX013, elevation 444 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 14: code WX014, elevation 481 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 15: code WX015, elevation 518 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 16: code WX016, elevation 555 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 17: code WX017, elevation 592 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 18: code WX018, elevation 629 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 19: code WX019, elevation 666 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 20: code WX020, elevation 703 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 21: code WX021, elevation 740 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 22: code WX022, elevation 777 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 23: code WX023, elevation 814 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 24: code WX024, elevation 851 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 25: code WX025, elevation 888 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 26: code WX026, elevation 25 m, report